KH0144,"For a complete listing of Ica quipus, see AS100.
(Ascher #2) By spacing, the quipe is separated into 2 gorups of 7 pendants each.  Both groups have the same color pattern: MB, EB, B, MB:W, B:W, W, W. 
(Ascher #3) With the exception of the first position, values in both groups are in the same relative order.  Specifically, Pi7 > Pi2 > Pi4 > Pi3 > Pi5 > Pi6  where i = 1, 2. 
(Ascher #4)  With the exception of the 6th position, the values of group 2 are greater than those in corresponding positions in group 1. 
(Ascher #5)  The last value in group 1 is the sum of 3 other values in the group:  P17 = P11 + P13 + P16 (where the numerals are to be read as subscripts--cjb).
(Ascher #6) a.  Two pairs of values in  group 1 have the same sum.  In both pairs, the values are 3 positions apart.  P11 + P14 = P13 + P16.  b)  With a discrepancy of 1, the sum is the same for a pair of values in corresponding positions in both groups.  P13 + P16 ~ P23 + P26 (again numerals to be read as subscripts--cjb)",quipu,False,False,False,False,False,False,False,False,False,False,False,False,False,False,False,False,False
KH0145,"AS130, AS154, AS155, AS177, and AS178 were acquired by the Museum in 1907 with provenance near Lima.  For a discussion of them see Ascher and Ascher 1987:850-851.
1. Construction note: The twisted end of cord 1 is linked through the twisted end of the main cord so that it dangles from the end of the main cord. (See diagram fo AS100)
3. The 16 pendants are 11 different colors. Only 1 color appears on more than 2 pendants. All pendants with the repeated color DB:W have subsidiaries that are YB and have the same value on the pendant as on the subsidiary. 
4. With the exception of the first pendant and its subsidiary, all values are 0-6.
5. The sum of the values on the first pendant and its subsidiary equals the sum of the values on the other 15 pendants and their subsidiaries.
6. Discussion of AS130, AS154, AS155, AS177, AS178, and associated blank quipu:
