KH0074,"1. Construction note: This is two quipus tied together.  Both main cords and all pendant cords are W.  The twisted end of the main cord A is bent back and slipped through the strands of itself forming a closed loop from which P1 and P2 are suspended.  The other end of main cord A is tied around main cord B. (See Ascher notes page 358.)
